.SH "NAME"
git-commit-deps \- Collect commit ranges and recursively expand DEPS and submodule rolls\&.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
\fIgit commit\-deps\fR [\-\-repo <path>] [\-\-format <format>] [\-\-include\-start]
                [\-\-first\-parent] [\-\-max\-level <int>]
                [\-n <int> | \-\-max\-count <int>] [\-\-filter <path\-or\-url>\&...]
                [\-\-fetch] [\-\-sync\-command] [<commit> [<commit>]]
.fi
.sp
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
\fBgit commit\-deps\fR collects commits in a Git commit range and recursively expands dependency rolls recorded in \fBDEPS\fR files and Git submodules (gitlinks) in monotonic post\-order\&.
.sp
Positional \fB<commit>\fR arguments support several forms:
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
Two\-dot ranges (\fB<start>\&.\&.<end>\fR) or two separate endpoints (\fB<start> <end>\fR), listing commits reachable from
\fB<end>\fR
excluding
\fB<start>\fR\&. Omitting either side of
\fB\&.\&.\fR
defaults to
\fBHEAD\fR
(for example,
\fBorigin/main\&.\&.\fR)\&.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
Three\-dot symmetric ranges (\fB<start>\&.\&.\&.<end>\fR), listing commits reachable from
\fB<end>\fR
since the merge\-base of
\fB<start>\fR
and
\fB<end>\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
A single commit (\fB<commit>\fR
or
\fB<commit>^!\fR), inspecting that commit alone, or walking
\fB<int>\fR
commits ending at
\fB<commit>\fR
when combined with
\fB\-n <int>\fR\&. When
\fB\-n <int>\fR
is given with no
\fB<commit>\fR, commits ending at
\fBHEAD\fR
are inspected\&.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
Chromium commit positions (\fBCr\-Commit\-Position\fR), such as
\fBrefs/heads/main@{#1412345}\fR,
\fBorigin/main@{#1412345}\fR,
\fB@{#1412345}\fR,
\fB\(aqCr\-Commit\-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1412345}\(aq\fR, or bare position numbers (for example,
\fB1412345\&.\&.1412400\fR)\&.
.RE
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\-\-repo <path>
.RS 4
Repository checkout path to inspect (default: current directory)\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-format <format>
.RS 4
Output format:
\fBtable\fR
(default),
\fBcsv\fR, or
\fBjson\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-include\-start
.RS 4
Include the start commit itself in the top\-level commit range\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-first\-parent
.RS 4
Follow only the first parent when traversing merge commits\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-max\-level <int>
.RS 4
Maximum subrepository recursion depth (\fB0\fR
inspects top\-level commits only)\&.
.RE
.PP
\-n <int>, \-\-max\-count <int>
.RS 4
Limit the number of top\-level commits inspected\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-filter <path\-or\-url>
.RS 4
Restrict subrepository roll expansion to matching dependency path(s) or repository URL(s)\&. Can be specified multiple times\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-fetch
.RS 4
Fetch missing rolled subrepository commits from
\fBorigin\fR
before expanding subrepository commit ranges\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-sync\-command, \-\-sync\-commands
.RS 4
Include the checkout command for each commit (\fBgclient sync \-\-revision <path>@<sha>\&.\&.\&.\fR
inside a
\fB\&.gclient\fR
workspace, or
\fBgit checkout \-\-detach <sha>\fR
in a standalone Git repository)\&.
.RE
.SH "EXAMPLE"
.sp
Expand all \fBDEPS\fR and submodule rolls in the last 10 commits, fetching any missing subrepository objects as needed:
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
git commit\-deps \-n 10 \-\-fetch
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.sp
Expand only \fBsrc/v8\fR rolls between two \fBCr\-Commit\-Position\fR numbers and emit JSON with \fBgclient sync\fR commands:
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
git commit\-deps 1412345\&.\&.1412400 \-\-filter src/v8 \-\-format json \-\-sync\-command
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.sp
Detach \fBHEAD\fR before syncing to a bisected revision set in a \fB\&.gclient\fR checkout:
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
git checkout \-\-detach && gclient sync \-R \-f \-D \-\-nohooks \-\-revision src@<sha> \-\-revision src/v8@<v8_sha>
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.sp
.SH "CAVEATS"
.sp
When bisecting inside a \fB\&.gclient\fR workspace with \fB\-\-sync\-command\fR, always detach \fBHEAD\fR in the root repository (and in any overridden subrepository on a local branch) by running \fBgit checkout \-\-detach\fR before invoking \fBgclient sync \-\-revision <path>@<sha>\fR\&. Running \fBgclient sync \-\-revision\fR while checked out on an attached local branch causes \fBgclient\fR to rebase that branch onto the target commit instead of checking out a detached state\&.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.sp
